    "reviews": [
      {
        "author_name": "Anna Garayt",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106245751364912891855/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJsZUsXUq1y_Es8qRhWnYUCs_W1htKqAjca5G4YoVMawuGwsw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "in the last week",
        "text": "very very VERY poor. do not recommend.\n\nI’m disappointed with my experience at this salon, especially given the prices they charge.\nThe space itself did not feel particularly clean, and the setup is very basic, which already sets expectations. Unfortunately, the service did not justify the cost either.\nFrom the beginning, the technician repeatedly tried to convince me not to choose a regular pedicure, insisting that it “dries too long,” despite me clearly stating my preference. My choice and needs were consistently disregarded in favor of what seemed easier for the technician, rather than what I requested.\nWhen the service was completed, the quality of the work was poor. The nail polish was applied unevenly, with visible lines and gaps. When I asked for it to be fixed, instead of correcting the application properly, a thick additional layer of polish was added. While this covered some gaps, it resulted in nails that looked uneven, lumpy, bubbly, and did not dry properly.\nAt the end, when I pointed out the poor result, I was told again that I should have chosen shellac because it dries faster. This reinforced the feeling that the focus was on the salon’s convenience, not on delivering the service I asked and paid for.\nFor a place with such basic facilities and relatively high prices, the quality of work and respect for customer preference were unacceptable. I would not consider this good value for money.\n_______\nupdate: on a day 5 polish started flaking off.. day 7- half is gone. for comparison, my usual life time of a nail polish on my toes- min 3 weeks",
        "time": 1770954897,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Sylvana Abdelnour",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104419558589822881563/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKyPayan8DJwfB-Lt1gEg2JczMItiyOzzPDjgRYZXrD_L412g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "4 months ago",
        "text": "I called ahead and was told $40 for a refill and $45 for French. When I arrived, I was asked if I wanted to do a pedicure and to remove my nails and do a whole new set instead, which I brushed off since I just wanted a refill. I showed the picture of the skinny French I wanted. The tech who did my nails had an aggressive attitude. She replaced one nail but made it wider than the rest, didn’t check that the lengths matched between hands, and the French lines were uneven. When I politely asked for a small fix, she said it would cost more because “this French is different and takes me a lot of time’’ even though that was never mentioned upfront. She also told me it couldn’t look like the picture because she’s “not a machine.” At one point, when I slightly moved my hand she snapped “don’t move,” and later when I noticed a hair from the towel and tried to get it off, she kept repeating every few seconds “be careful, be careful, the hair don’t move” as if I was the problem messing up my own nails. At the end, she even told me if I didn’t like it, I could just go somewhere else. Overall, very careless work and poor customer service. I left disappointed and won’t be returning.",
        "time": 1758991543,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Nathalie Seguin",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115203738588503988815/reviews",
        "language": "en",
